A||N||7||turbo86se||cleaning lugnuts||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||06-08-2001||12:00 PM||||<BR>Anyone know of good methods to clean the insides of lugnuts? Some of mine are stained with a "rust" color b/c the factory wrench I used was wet and the paint was scraped off. <BR>TIA!  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||01:04 PM||||I use some wd40, a wire brush dremel attachment, and a paper towell...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-08-2001||03:39 PM||||dont you have the plastic nut covers?<P> you know you are spending way too much time on your car, when you pull the wheel off for some reason, and you clean the plastic nuts covers with ArmorAll before you put them back on (c%||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||06-08-2001||05:43 PM||||Well, I took a lugnut off, they're the one's where you need a special socket to get them off, not like conventional ones, they're hollow, and you can see the stud. Here's what I noticed, the studs are producing the rust discoloration. Real nasty when they get wet. I guess I could remove the wheel, brush the studs down with a wire brush, and paint them with Rust-olem. Sound good?<BR>Any other suggestions?<BR>TIA!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||06-08-2001||06:30 PM||||I wouldn't paint the studs.  I did that on my jeep and it was almost like I put loctite on the damn thinks.  $0.02||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||06-08-2001||07:59 PM||||Don't paint them. Don't oil/grease them either. the oil/grease can make them work loose.<P>The lugs are going to rust.... If you are worried they could sieze the use anit sieze on the threads ONLY. A little bit goes a long way. Unlike oil/grease the antisieze won't wick/run onto other surfaces.<P>DO NOT allow the antisieze to get on the cone face of the lugs or the lug holes in the wheel. Nothing should be used on that sureface ever or you could have the lugs come loose. The cone face is what locks the lugs against vibration.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||06-09-2001||12:30 AM||||Turbo, Iam going to include something cool for your t-tops that you most likely need (no cost to you).  You will just have to wait until the package arrives.  Ya, the suspence is killing you!!||||reg||1
